      {
        "id": 187719,
        "name": "MigrantP",
        "username": "MigrantP",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/migrantp/{size}/1921_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-01-04T01:44:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Sorry&nbsp;robb8888, but that's all basically a product of your imagination.</p><p>Nothing can happen in a Weekly One-Shot that cannot happen in any game you play with the same setup.</p><p>There is no Weekly One-Shot where there is \"*one* combination\" and \"no room for error\" in order to win. All you have to do is read the threads here and on Steam and that would be obvious; people beat them in all kinds of ways.</p><p>The vast majority of Weekly One-Shots have no specific setup in mind at all, and were just a random game I tried and felt had a reasonable challenge level.</p><p>The ones that do have a specific setup are typically very limited, to something like the first two cards the villain plays.</p><p>There are literally zero Weekly One-Shots where I have in some way planned for there to be a certain way you're supposed to beat it. I cannot imagine ever bothering to try to set up a game like that.</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:13:33.345Z",
