      {
        "id": 187723,
        "name": "schadkehnfreude",
        "username": "schadkehnfreude",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/schadkehnfreude/{size}/2357_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-01-04T15:06:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"robb8888\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> robb8888:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;Is the whole point of these things just to assume that the strategies one would normally employ won't work, and to start every game by experimenting with something bizarre, hoping that first time you'll luck upon the unusual combination that will get past the bad draws/bad deck lineup? &nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I mean, my unconventional strategy was first dropping equipment to kill Citizen Truth ASAP (twice! oy vey!) and then controlling the deck with Infrared and trying not to die and dumping as much damage on Dawn as possible. &nbsp;=\\</p>\n<p>Thing is, no matter how many games with the same lineup you run beforehand, those won't tell you anything you don't already know if you've ever played with those decks before. &nbsp;You know what's in Fanatic's deck. &nbsp;You know what Insula Primus plays. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>But at the End of Days, you gotta play the cards on the table/hand, not the cards in the deck. &nbsp;In my case I double-skipped once with Fanatic which drew me into my game-winning play. &nbsp;Someone else did that and End of Days'd, which I didn't. &nbsp;Someone else instead used Chastise—&gt;Zealous Offense to control the field. &nbsp;All three approaches were valid lines of play within what was given to us. &nbsp;Generally there's enough to work with in the one-shots that you can overcome what the villain throws at you</p>\n<p>(The Dark Watch vs Matriarch was still some grade-A bullshit, though <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> )</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:13:33.650Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
