      {
        "id": 187724,
        "name": "seesome",
        "username": "seesome",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/seesome/{size}/2018_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-01-04T23:43:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Mint</p><p>Like others, I played the Razor and Cannon to weaken Truth, then skipped Fanatic's turn due to her cards being situationally useless. Drew EoD and decided to sacrifice Wraith and Bunker's weapons to wipe the board. &nbsp;On round two, I played an Ammo Drop, so Bunker could stock up on cards when EoD triggered.&nbsp;<span>That gave me lots of choices thereafter and B was able to use his base power (which I usually ignore) to keep taking out Dawn's ongoings.&nbsp;</span></p><p>I took a lot of damage from a round with Cit Winter, Cit Hammer, and an Obsidian Field, but that set up a Wrathful Retribution which took Dawn down to the 20s. After clearing them, I just kept hitting Dawn while ignoring the other citizens so Dawn wouldn't flip. &nbsp;</p><p>Fanatic had her resurrection trigger. Wraith got out the Smoke Bombs, which combined with Bunker's plating for some good DR until Wraith went down, at which point she kept healing Fanatic until F had more HP than Dawn. After that, the pair of T-Rexes munched Dawn to bits.</p><p>The unconventional thing for me was NOT playing Wraith's Infrared Goggles! Usually those go right into play, especially against Dawn. But in this game I felt like other choices were always a bit more pressing.</p>",
        "post_number": 27,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:13:33.725Z",
